{"data": [{"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-27T02:08:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114902088899539416"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 161, "start": 155, "tag": "China"}], "urls": [{"description": "Beijing's economic model conceals the mistakes that free markets expose.", "display_url": "washingtonpost.com/opinions/2026/…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2026/10/21/china-model-has-an-accounting-problem", "images": [{"height": 960, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113063831690006528/fVbx3kzF?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1440}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113063831690006528/fVbx3kzF?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "Opinion | China can manipulate statistics. It can’t fool markets forever.", "unwound_url": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2026/10/21/china-model-has-an-accounting-problem", "url": "https://t.co/bvmvyojjXY"}]}, "id": "2114902088899539416", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2726, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "\"A good reason to be skeptical is that the 🇨🇳 govt has stopped publishing the granular data needed to independently assess the true state of its economy...#China's opacity is a serious weakness bc functioning markets depend on trustworthy info\"\n\nIndeed\nhttps://t.co/bvmvyojjXY", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114902088899539416"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-27T01:44:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114896046182854730"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/carlquintanill…", "end": 176, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/carlquintanilla/status/2114684511829057661", "start": 153, "url": "https://t.co/KzDyP545cx"}]}, "id": "2114896046182854730", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 19, "impression_count": 4305, "like_count": 42, "quote_count": 0, "reply_